WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:05.190
Sheev Palpatine, a.k.a. Darth Sidious, has
always been an enigmatic character in Star

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:09.160
Wars lore, and much of his role in the saga
remains shrouded in mystery.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:13.240
After his unexpected return at the end of
the Disney sequel trilogy, let's unearth some

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.740
facts about the evil Emperor you might not
know.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:21.060
A few years ago, one of the longest-running
Star Wars fan theories was finally confirmed:

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:24.460
Yes, Darth Sidious really did create Anakin
Skywalker.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:26.780
All of the clues had been there for a while,
of course.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:31.500
In The Phantom Menace, Anakin's mother Shmi
tells Qui-Gon Jinn that she became pregnant

00:00:31.509 --> 00:00:35.510
with Anakin without the help of a father,
while Qui-Gon discovers that young Anakin

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:37.830
has an abnormally high midi-chlorian count.

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:42.850
In Revenge of the Sith, Palpatine tells Anakin
the story of his former master, Darth Plagueis,

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:45.780
who figured out how to use midi-chlorians
to create life.

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:51.100
According to the movie's making-of book, Lucas
actually wrote a scene making Anakin's parentage

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:53.560
explicit, but the lines were cut from the
final film.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:59.020
Years later, in 2018, the 25th issue of Marvel's
Darth Vader comic series settled the matter

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:03.440
by apparently showing Vader dwelling on the
actual moment that Palpatine as Darth Sidious

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:06.180
zapped his mother's womb with dark side energy.

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:10.380
There's enough wiggle room built in that Lucasfilm
could retcon this if they want, but for now

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:13.540
it's pretty clear: Palpatine is Darth Vader's
daddy.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.900
Not many Star Wars fans are aware of Emperor
Palpatine's true connection with the Jedi

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:18.400
Temple.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:22.440
Thousands of years before the formation of
the Galactic Republic, the Sith erected a

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:25.880
shrine on the planet Coruscant that emitted
dark side energy.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:30.660
After defeating the Sith, the Jedi Order built
the Jedi Temple directly over the foundations

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:31.700
of the Sith shrine.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:35.920
This was done for two different reasons to
symbolically bury the legacy of the Sith and

00:01:35.939 --> 00:01:38.979
to neutralize the dark energy that the shrine
radiated.

00:01:38.979 --> 00:01:43.029
However, after Darth Sidious defeated the
Jedi order, he converted what was left of

00:01:43.029 --> 00:01:47.980
the Jedi temple into his personal Imperial
Palace and secretly excavated the Sith shrine.

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:52.300
Palpatine had the unearthing of the shrine
completed entirely by droids so that even

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:54.580
Lord Vader would not be aware of its existence.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:58.819
The Emperor used the refurbished Sith shrine
as his own private sanctum where he could

00:01:58.819 --> 00:02:02.840
meditate on the dark side of the Force, and
was eventually planning on allowing Vader

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:03.560
to join him.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:07.860
Together, he believed they could use the shrine's
connection to the dark side to discover more

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.340
Sith knowledge and powers.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:14.100
Palpatine had no remorse for the people of
his own home planet when he planned Operation

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:18.960
Cinder, a contingency plan to ensure the longevity
of the Galactic Empire should he ever be killed.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:22.720
Palpatine believed that if the Empire was
unable to prevent his assassination, then

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:26.790
the entire organization was a failure and
did not deserve to live on without him.

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:31.260
In order to fulfill his vision, Palpatine
created a plan to annihilate both the Empire

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:35.930
and its enemies should he ever perish, and
entrusted a select group of Imperial officers

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:38.130
with the duty of rebuilding a new Empire.

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:42.720
The plan was to use a series of satellites
to form a climate disruption array capable

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:46.860
of laying waste to resistance-allied planets
with catastrophic weather events.

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:50.760
After the Emperor's apparent death during
the Battle of Endor, one of these climate

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:55.260
disruption arrays was used to wreak havoc
upon Palpatine's home planet of Naboo . The

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:59.980
satellites created massive hurricanes and
electrical storms that ravaged the surface

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:00.820
of the planet.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:04.820
It was only through the actions of Leia Organa
and Lando Calrissian that the rebels were

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:09.370
able to destroy the climate disruption arrays
and stop the people of Naboo from being completely

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:10.300
wiped out.

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:15.320
Darth Sidious was a master Sith user and skilled
fighter, but he didn't take over the Republic

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:15.940
by force.

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:17.560
He used trickery and deceit.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:22.360
As such, it's hardly surprising that Palpatine
used his gift for psychological manipulation

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:26.160
well before he was on the way to becoming
Emperor, nor that he was one of the Galactic

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:27.610
Senate's most skilled propagandists.

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:32.230
Palpatine's predecessor, Supreme Chancellor
Valorum , was a weak-willed and indecisive

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:35.190
leader who often kowtowed to special interests.

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:36.770
In short, he wasn't up to the job.

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:40.900
So, when Valorum needed to sway the hearts
and minds of the people, he often offloaded

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:43.900
his duties to everyone's favorite Sith-lord-in-hiding.

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:48.220
The book Star Wars Propaganda, a collection
of in-universe propaganda pieces, has some

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:53.470
of Palpatine's work, including a striking
invitation to the Republic's 1,000 year anniversary

00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:54.040
celebration.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:58.680
Palpatine didn't stop meddling in the Republic's
propaganda machine after he took power, either.

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:02.990
When the Republic commissioned posters to
bolster support for the Clone Wars, Palpatine

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:06.700
explicitly forbade artists from producing
materials featuring the Jedi.

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:10.510
Publicly, Palpatine said that he didn't want
to make the Jedi, who were already wary about

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:12.660
being military leaders, more uncomfortable.

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:17.080
Privately, Palpatine didn't want people siding
with the Jedi, since he planned to scapegoat

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:19.320
them as part of his coup once the war ended.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:21.440
Death wasn't the end for Palpatine.

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:25.200
Even after he died on the second Death Star,
his plans lived on.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:29.600
Years before Palpatine crowned himself Emperor,
he established an underground "observatory"

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:32.720
on the planet Jakku, Rey's homeworld in The
Force Awakens.

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:33.220
His plan?

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:37.320
Stuff it full of Sith relics with the power
to cause an explosion and then, in the event

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:41.380
of his death, detonate the whole thing and
wipe out the Empire and the Rebel Alliance

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:42.520
in one fell swoop.

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:47.580
Palpatine figured any Empire that was inept
enough to let him die didn't deserve to survive,

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:51.860
and winnowing out the Empire's weaker elements
would give it the freedom to reform into something

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:52.360
stronger.

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:54.600
If his enemies died in the explosion too?

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:55.440
So much the better.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:05:00.240
Palpatine put a man named Gallius Rax in charge
of the plan, which unfolds in Chuck Wendig's

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:01.860
Aftermath trilogy of books.

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:02.980
It almost works.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:07.460
Rax manages to lure the Empire and the New
Republic to Jakku for a final showdown, but

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:10.220
a team of good and bad guys stop the planet
from blowing up.

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:14.700
Still, after the battle, the Empire heads
off to the Unknown Regions to regroup, where

00:05:14.701 --> 00:05:17.450
it transforms into the lean and mean First
Order.

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:19.100
In the long term, mission accomplished.

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:24.340
Palpatine looked down on luxury, preferring
a spartan lifestyle that fit with his brutal

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:25.300
Sith philosophy.

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:30.100
Discomfort isn't great for impressing politicians,
however, so Palpatine also maintained his

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:32.620
own pleasure craft, which he called the Imperialis.

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:37.360
He must've loved the ship a lot, too every
single one of Palpatine's secret observatories,

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:41.650
which were home to the Sith lord's most treasured
artifacts, contained a full replica of the

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:42.140
craft.

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:46.960
The Imperialis was fast enough to outmaneuver
a Star Destroyer, had all kinds of fancy weapons

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:51.150
and defensive tools, and was stuffed full
of treasure, making it a perfect target for

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:55.380
smugglers and pirates those who were dumb
enough to take on the Emperor himself, anyway.

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:58.389
Well, that description fits Lando Calrissian
perfectly.

00:05:58.389 --> 00:06:03.760
In Marvel's Lando comic miniseries, Mr. Calrissian
boosts the Imperialis and ends up on Palpatine's

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:04.420
bad side.

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:08.960
While Palpatine sends Star Destroyers and
bounty hunters after Lando, none of them can

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:12.650
bring the Imperialis home, so Palpatine orders
the ship destroyed.

00:06:12.650 --> 00:06:15.340
Lando escapes, but the Imperialis is lost
forever.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:20.400
The dark robes, saggy pale skin, and yellow
eyes should've given it away, but even after

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:25.010
Palpatine transformed the Republic into the
Empire, he worked very hard to hide his Sith

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:25.560
background.

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:30.020
People knew or, at the very least, rumors
suggested that Darth Vader was familiar with

00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:31.180
the ways of the Force.

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:34.190
That Palpatine was his master was a tightly-guarded
secret.

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:38.460
According to the books Lords of the Sith and
Tarkin, only a few people were privy to what

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:39.480
Palpatine was.

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:44.020
His apprentices Darth Maul, Count Dooku, and
Darth Vader they all knew, of course.

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:45.060
So did his royal guards.

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:47.180
Almost everyone else was kept in the dark.

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:52.080
Even Grand Moff Tarkin, one of Palpatine's
closest allies and most trusted confidants,

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:54.270
only suspected that Palpatine was a Sith.

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:55.490
He didn't know for sure.

00:06:55.490 --> 00:06:59.820
It's not clear why Palpatine didn't flaunt
his Sith heritage, although it's easy to guess.

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:03.300
For one, Palpatine spent his entire career
operating in the shadows.

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:04.930
Why start moving into the light now?

00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:07.440
For another, to Palpatine, information was
power.

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:10.160
There's no use in telling people more than
they need to know.

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:12.940
Every fact that's revealed can eventually
be used against you.

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:18.320
Lots of Palpatine's backstory comes from James
Luceno's Darth Plagueis, which is no longer

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:22.090
considered canonical in Disney's new, streamlined
Star Wars Universe.

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:24.639
Still, Plagueis' legacy lives on in a few
ways.

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:29.570
"Did you ever hear the tragedy of Darth Plagueis
the Wise?"

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:34.380
Plagueis' desire to conquer death plays a
major role in Anakin's turn to the dark side,

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:39.320
and could be a key factor in Palpatine's mysterious,
unexplained return in The Rise of Skywalker.

00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:44.060
Finally, while Palpatine killed Plagueis while
his master slept, he did take a souvenir with

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:47.560
him 11-4D, Plagueis' trusty protocol droid.

00:07:48.020 --> 00:07:50.940
Palpatine didn't establish the Empire to get
famous.

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:51.880
He just wanted power.

00:07:51.940 --> 00:07:55.980
While serving as a senator made Palpatine
a celebrity, he retreated from the public

00:07:55.980 --> 00:08:00.260
eye once he became emperor, letting the Imperial
Ruling Council handle most of the day-to-day

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:04.600
work of governing and leaving nastier tasks
up to his apprentice, Darth Vader.

00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:08.900
As a result, Palpatine was safe from his enemies
and could devote as much time as he wanted

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:13.311
to his own pursuits, but it had an unintended
side effect: Because no one saw him, some

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:16.180
conspiracy theorists argued that Palpatine
was dead.

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:19.960
The most common story alleged that the Jedi
killed Palpatine during their "uprising,"

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:24.500
and that the Imperial leaders were using Palpatine's
name to grab power for themselves.

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:27.140
The Empire tried to dispel these rumors in
a few ways.

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:31.960
In Tarkin, Tarkin's friend Nils Tenant admits
that the Ruling Council sent out fake flying

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:36.530
motorcades to make it look like Palpatine
was traveling from place to place.

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:40.570
In Aftermath, we learn that the Empire used
body doubles to give the impression that Palpatine

00:08:40.570 --> 00:08:43.380
was giving speeches or making other public
appearances.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:47.660
In reality, however, Palpatine preferred to
stay at home although he was very much alive.

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:52.180
Like Darth Plagueis before him, Palpatine
was obsessed with unlocking the secrets of

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:55.860
immortality, which clearly came into play
during The Rise of Skywalker.

00:08:55.940 --> 00:08:58.180
However, not all of his experiments paid off.

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:02.260
Just look at what happened to Project Blackwing:
instead of discovering the key to everlasting

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:05.630
life, the Empire accidentally created stormtrooper
zombies.

00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:09.390
In the mobile game Star Wars: Commander which
is canon, because under Disney, everything

00:09:09.390 --> 00:09:14.300
is Palpatine recruits a bunch of "Sith scientists"
to make Imperial soldiers live forever.

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:18.600
Instead, they create a virus that turns the
corpses into members of the living dead.

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:22.960
The virus ultimately creates an entire army
of so-called Death Troopers, but the combined

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:27.320
forces of the Empire and the Rebel Alliance
contain the outbreak, saving the galaxy from

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:28.420
a zombie apocalypse.

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:31.570
Still, the Death Troopers' legacy lives on
in one key way.

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:35.550
Allegedly, the Death Troopers seen in Rogue
One who were special ops soldiers, not zombies

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:37.940
got their name from Palpatine's failed experiment.

00:09:38.060 --> 00:09:39.080
Hey, it's a good name.

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:40.260
May as well use it twice.

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:44.000
Don't let anyone tell you that Palpatine didn't
have a sense of humor.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:45.960
The way he treated the Senate proves that
he does.

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:49.540
Despite what you might think, Palpatine didn't
dissolve the Galactic Senate as soon as he

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:50.200
took power.

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:52.340
In fact, he kept it around for decades.

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:56.660
Before the Death Star, Palpatine saw the Senate
as a valuable political tool that let its

00:09:56.660 --> 00:10:00.870
constituents feel like they had some say in
politics as a means of quashing potential

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:05.480
rebellions, even though he had all the power,
that’s why he said “I am the senate!”.

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:07.080
It was an illusion, of course.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:11.500
Over time, power moved from the Senate to
local, regional leaders, robbing the politicians

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:12.700
of any real influence.

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:16.920
Once Palpatine created the Death Star, which
would let him control the galaxy via fear

00:10:16.930 --> 00:10:21.040
instead of politics, he disbanded the Senate
entirely, but that didn't happen until the

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:22.180
beginning of A New Hope.

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:25.480
That whole time, nobody bothered to let the
senators know what was happening.

00:10:25.480 --> 00:10:26.220
"Wait a minute!

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:27.540
How did this happen?

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:28.340
We're smarter than this."

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:32.730
In a comic in the ninth issue of Star Wars
Rebels Magazine, the crew of the Ghost runs

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:36.760
into a senator from the planet Thrad, who
still believes in the legislative body.

00:10:36.920 --> 00:10:39.140
The senators still debate policy, she says.

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:42.760
They still pass bills, which they send to
Palpatine to be signed into law.

00:10:42.779 --> 00:10:45.550
They don't realize that Palpatine simply ignores
them.

00:10:45.550 --> 00:10:47.250
They think they're making a difference.

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:51.300
Instead, they're frittering away in the Senate
chamber, doing absolutely nothing.

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:52.460
Heartbreaking?

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:53.200
Kind of.

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:54.440
Tragically hilarious?

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:55.660
Oh, absolutely.

